<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Contents of Appendix</span></p>
</div><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:1px;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>LLM Usage Statement</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, Large Language Models (LLMs) were primarily used for text refinement, such as improving the clarity of writing. In addition, for the ESCI experiments, the chain-of-thought (CoT) data was generated using Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct through rejection sampling.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To better understand the empirical phenomena observed in §<a href="#S3" title="3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we provide a theoretical analysis from the perspective of information theory. Our goal is to explain <span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Finding</span> <a href="#f1" title="Finding 1: Smaller learning rates achieve a more favorable trade-off. ‣ 3.2 Main Results ‣ 3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold">1</a> and <a href="#f2" title="Finding 2: Label-only supervision loosens learning rate constraints for Pareto-optimal trade-offs. ‣ 3.2 Main Results ‣ 3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_bold">2</a> mentioned in §<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Main Results ‣ 3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>. To this end, we first introduce several compression-based tools that form the basis of our analysis. We then apply these tools to shed light on the two key findings highlighted earlier.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Preliminaries</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Supervised Fine-tuning (SFT).</span> In SFT, the LLM is trained on a labeled dataset <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}=\{(x^{(i)},y^{(i)})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}=\{(x^{(i)},y^{(i)})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is a natural language prompt (e.g., an instruction or question), and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=(y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{T_{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=(y_{1},y_{2},\dots,y_{T_{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the corresponding target response, represented as a sequence of tokens. The objective of SFT is to maximize the conditional likelihood of the target sequence <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> given the input <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, which corresponds to minimizing the following negative log-likelihood loss:
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}(\theta)=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T_{y}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mtext>SFT</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{SFT}}(\theta)=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}_{\text{SFT}}}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{T_{y}}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the model’s output distribution over the vocabulary, and <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{&lt;t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{&lt;t}</annotation></semantics></math> is previous target tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lossless Compression.</span>
In lossless compression, the goal is to encode a sequence of symbols <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=(x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=(x_{1},x_{2},\dots,x_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from a source distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> into a binary representation without any loss of information, such that the original sequence can be perfectly reconstructed. According to Shannon’s source coding theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shannon, 1948</a>)</cite>, the limit of compression is given by the Shannon entropy of the source: <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P}\big[-\log P(x)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P}\big[-\log P(x)\big]</annotation></semantics></math>, which specifies the minimum expected number of bits per symbol needed for encoding.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LLM Modeling is Compression.</span> Given a dataset <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from the true distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and a model distribution <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected code length under arithmetic coding <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Witten et al., 1987</a>)</cite> is given by <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(P,Q):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P}\big[-\log Q(x)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(P,Q):=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim P}\big[-\log Q(x)\big]</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, minimizing the log-likelihood loss directly corresponds to reducing the expected compression rate when the model is employed as a lossless compressor <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deletang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hutter, 2005</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>LLM Compression Protocol</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal is to analyze the dynamics of domain-specific SFT. Motivated by the equivalence between language modeling and data compression <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deletang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, we view an LLM as a <em id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">compressor</em>, where the effectiveness of training can be measured through changes in code length. In this view, improvements or degradations in performance across datasets correspond to variations in compression rate. Below, we formalize this perspective by introducing the notion of token trees and describing the LLM compression protocol in our context.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="116.63" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 116.63" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,116.63) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#478978;" fill="#478978" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 110.73 C 0 113.99 2.64 116.63 5.91 116.63 L 555.16 116.63 C 558.43 116.63 561.07 113.99 561.07 110.73 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F8FEFC;" fill="#F8FEFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 110.73 C 1.97 112.9 3.73 114.66 5.91 114.66 L 555.16 114.66 C 557.34 114.66 559.1 112.9 559.1 110.73 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 95.98)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="96.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Token Tree <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For a dataset <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{z_{i}\in\mathcal{V}^{\infty}\mid i=1,2,\ldots\},\quad|\mathcal{V}|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.167em" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{z_{i}\in\mathcal{V}^{\infty}\mid i=1,2,\ldots\},\quad|\mathcal{V}|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>,
where <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\{v_{1},v_{2},\ldots,v_{|\mathcal{V}|}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\{v_{1},v_{2},\ldots,v_{|\mathcal{V}|}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite vocabulary of size <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math>,
the token tree of <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, denoted as <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined as follows: (1) each node has <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{V}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{V}|</annotation></semantics></math> child nodes labeled <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{1},v_{2},\ldots,v_{|\mathcal{V}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{1},v_{2},\ldots,v_{|\mathcal{V}|}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with an
end-of-sequence (EOS) leaf node; (2) The weight of a non-leaf node is the sum of the weights of all its child nodes; (3) The path from the root to an EOS leaf node defines a response <math id="A2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, with the corresponding EOS node weight representing the response’s probability.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="116.63" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 116.63" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,116.63) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#478978;" fill="#478978" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 110.73 C 0 113.99 2.64 116.63 5.91 116.63 L 555.16 116.63 C 558.43 116.63 561.07 113.99 561.07 110.73 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F8FEFC;" fill="#F8FEFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 110.73 C 1.97 112.9 3.73 114.66 5.91 114.66 L 555.16 114.66 C 557.34 114.66 559.1 112.9 559.1 110.73 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 95.98)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:6.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="96.09" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(LLM Compression Protocol)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the token tree of dataset <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let
<math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the conditional distribution over
<math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}\cup\{\mathrm{EOS}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∪</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">EOS</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}\cup\{\mathrm{EOS}\}</annotation></semantics></math> predicted by an LLM with parameters <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>
at node <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given a response <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> (a path from the root to an EOS leaf, truncated to a pre-defined maximum depth <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>),
the LLM compression protocol encodes <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> using <em id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">arithmetic coding</em>,
where at each step the coding probabilities are given by
<math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> for the current node <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> along the path of <math id="A2.Thmdefinition2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark:</span> The truncation to a maximum depth <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> reflects practical constraints in the use
of large language models. For example, responses are usually limited to a fixed
context window, and generated sequences are typically
bounded in length.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expected Code Length)<span id="A2.Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider a finite parameter model <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and a token tree
<math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> truncated to depth <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the compression protocol of Definition <a href="#S3.Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 3.2 (LLM Compression Protocol). ‣ 3.3 Theoretical Analysis ‣ 3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>, the expected code length of a random response <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{z\sim P}[L_{\theta}(z)]=-\sum_{l=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{|\mathcal{V}|^{\,l-1}}p_{l,j}\,\log q_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{z\sim P}[L_{\theta}(z)]=-\sum_{l=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{|\mathcal{V}|^{\,l-1}}p_{l,j}\,\log q_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the distribution over responses, <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the probability assigned to the leaf node <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math> (the <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th node at layer <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>), and <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability assigned to the node <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math> by the model <math id="A2.Thmproposition1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Joint Token Tree for Multiple Datasets)<span id="A2.Thmproposition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> pairwise disjoint datasets <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{D}_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1},\ldots,\mathcal{D}_{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, each with its own token tree <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\bigcup_{i=1}^{N}\mathcal{D}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\bigcup_{i=1}^{N}\mathcal{D}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the union dataset, and let <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote its token tree. For each node <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math>, the node weight in <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> is given by <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\mathcal{D}}_{l,j}=(\sum_{i=1}^{N}|\mathcal{D}_{i}|p^{\mathcal{D}_{i}}_{l,j})\,/\,(\sum_{i=1}^{N}|\mathcal{D}_{i}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\mathcal{D}}_{l,j}=(\sum_{i=1}^{N}|\mathcal{D}_{i}|p^{\mathcal{D}_{i}}_{l,j})\,/\,(\sum_{i=1}^{N}|\mathcal{D}_{i}|)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\mathcal{D}_{i}}_{l,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\mathcal{D}_{i}}_{l,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is the node weight in <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{D}_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{D}_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of responses
in dataset <math id="A2.Thmproposition2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmproposition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmproposition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expected Code Length Discrepancy under Model Shift)<span id="A2.Thmproposition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider two model distributions <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{1}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{1}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{2}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{2}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> over the token tree
<math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> with distribution <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.
The change in expected code length on <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> when shifting from <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim P}[L_{q_{\theta_{2}}}(z)]-\mathbb{E}_{z\sim P}[L_{q_{\theta_{1}}}(z)]=-\sum_{l=1}^{d}\sum_{j}p_{l,j}\,\log\tfrac{q^{(2)}_{l,j}}{q^{(1)}_{l,j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim P}[L_{q_{\theta_{2}}}(z)]-\mathbb{E}_{z\sim P}[L_{q_{\theta_{1}}}(z)]=-\sum_{l=1}^{d}\sum_{j}p_{l,j}\,\log\tfrac{q^{(2)}_{l,j}}{q^{(1)}_{l,j}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Equivalently, <math id="A2.Thmproposition3.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P)=\mathrm{KL}\!\left(P\,\|\,q_{\theta_{2}}\right)-\mathrm{KL}\!\left(P\,\|\,q_{\theta_{1}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P)=\mathrm{KL}\!\left(P\,\|\,q_{\theta_{2}}\right)-\mathrm{KL}\!\left(P\,\|\,q_{\theta_{1}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the above, we adopt the expected code length as a surrogate metric for an LLM’s modeling quality on a given dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deletang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Specifically, reductions in code length discrepancy indicate better alignment between the model distribution and the data distribution, whereas increases suggest deterioration. This perspective will serve as the foundation for our subsequent analysis.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Approximating Fine-tuning Dynamics with Exponential Tilting</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our goal in this part is to uncover the behavior of LLMs during domain-specific fine-tuning. <span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Fine-tuning alters the conditional distributions assigned to each node in the token tree</span>, thereby shifting the model’s alignment with the data distribution. For analytical simplicity, we view fine-tuning at a high level as introducing perturbations to the probability assigned to each token node. To approximate these dynamics, we adopt the lens of <em id="A2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exponential tilting</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Maity et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, which captures how the distribution is reweighted under incremental updates.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Note that, exponential tilting is not strictly equivalent to SFT; rather, it serves as an <span id="A2.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">analytical surrogate that enables us to extract insights and motivation about the mechanisms</span> driving general-performance degradation and domain adaptation. In the following, we formalize the exponential tilting formulation and present how it approximates the token-level probability shifts induced by fine-tuning. We then provide error estimates that quantify the gap.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup.</span> We consider a pretrained LLM with distribution <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, which already models the dataset <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> well.
The model is then fine-tuned on a new dataset <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a node <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in the token tree <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{D}_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\hat{p}_{2}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{2}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the empirical target distribution induced by <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and let <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the model distribution at step <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> during fine-tuning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Full support via mild smoothing)<span id="A2.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To avoid support collapse, the target used in each step is defined as a smoothed mixture <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)=(1-\alpha)\,\hat{p}_{2}(\cdot\mid u)+\alpha\,\rho_{t}(\cdot\mid u),\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>α</mi><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)=(1-\alpha)\,\hat{p}_{2}(\cdot\mid u)+\alpha\,\rho_{t}(\cdot\mid u),\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\rho_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> is a strictly positive reference distribution (e.g., the current model <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> or the uniform distribution).
Hence <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}(a\mid u)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(a\mid u)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all tokens <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Small step in distribution space)<span id="A2.Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Each update is small at the distribution level: <math id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)\ \leq\ \varepsilon,\varepsilon\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)\ \leq\ \varepsilon,\varepsilon\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothness / finite tree)<span id="A2.Thmassumption3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.Thmassumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q_{\theta}(a\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q_{\theta}(a\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is twice continuously differentiable in <math id="A2.Thmassumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> with bounded second derivatives in a neighborhood of <math id="A2.Thmassumption3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>; vocabulary and depth are finite. Consequently, Taylor remainders are <math id="A2.Thmassumption3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\|\theta_{t+1}-\theta_{t}\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="110.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 110.29" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,110.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#478978;" fill="#478978" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 104.38 C 0 107.65 2.64 110.29 5.91 110.29 L 555.16 110.29 C 558.43 110.29 561.07 107.65 561.07 104.38 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F8FEFC;" fill="#F8FEFC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 104.38 C 1.97 106.56 3.73 108.32 5.91 108.32 L 555.16 108.32 C 557.34 108.32 559.1 106.56 559.1 104.38 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 89.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:5.74em;font-size:10pt;" height="89.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exponential Tilting Update)<span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For any non-leaf prefix <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in the token tree <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> and a step parameter <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>,
define the log-ratio <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{u}(a)\triangleq\log\!\big(\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)/q_{t}(a\mid u)\big),a\in\mathcal{V}\cup\{\mathrm{EOS}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≜</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒱</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∪</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">EOS</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{u}(a)\triangleq\log\!\big(\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)/q_{t}(a\mid u)\big),a\in\mathcal{V}\cup\{\mathrm{EOS}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. The <em id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">exponential tilting update</em> at prefix <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> is given by</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{q}_{t+1}(a\mid u)=\frac{q_{t}(a\mid u)\,\exp\{\lambda\,r_{u}(a)\}}{\sum_{b}q_{t}(b\mid u)\,\exp\{\lambda\,r_{u}(b)\}}=\frac{q_{t}(a\mid u)^{\,1-\lambda}\,\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)^{\,\lambda}}{\sum_{b}q_{t}(b\mid u)^{\,1-\lambda}\,\tilde{p}_{2,t}(b\mid u)^{\,\lambda}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> 1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> 1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{q}_{t+1}(a\mid u)=\frac{q_{t}(a\mid u)\,\exp\{\lambda\,r_{u}(a)\}}{\sum_{b}q_{t}(b\mid u)\,\exp\{\lambda\,r_{u}(b)\}}=\frac{q_{t}(a\mid u)^{\,1-\lambda}\,\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)^{\,\lambda}}{\sum_{b}q_{t}(b\mid u)^{\,1-\lambda}\,\tilde{p}_{2,t}(b\mid u)^{\,\lambda}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The boundary cases are consistent: <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> recovers <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1</annotation></semantics></math> recovers <math id="A2.Thmdefinition3.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="140.8" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 140.8" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,140.8) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 134.89 C 0 138.16 2.64 140.8 5.91 140.8 L 555.16 140.8 C 558.43 140.8 561.07 138.16 561.07 134.89 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 134.89 C 1.97 137.07 3.73 138.83 5.91 138.83 L 555.16 138.83 C 557.34 138.83 559.1 137.07 559.1 134.89 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 120.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:8em;font-size:10pt;" height="120.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS3.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First-order approximation by exponential tilting)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix a prefix <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the current model distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> and the smoothed target distribution <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the local <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|g\|_{t,u}:=\big(\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)}[g(a)^{2}]\big)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.0835em" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g\|_{t,u}:=\big(\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)}[g(a)^{2}]\big)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the standing assumptions, there exists an effective step size <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t,u}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Big\|\log q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)-\Big[(1-\lambda_{t,u})\,\log q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)+\lambda_{t,u}\,\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)-\psi_{t,u}\Big]\Big\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.0835em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big\|\log q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)-\Big[(1-\lambda_{t,u})\,\log q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)+\lambda_{t,u}\,\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)-\psi_{t,u}\Big]\Big\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t,u}</annotation></semantics></math> is the log-normalizer and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL trust-region radius such that <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)\ \leq\ \varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)\ \leq\ \varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The proof can be found in §<a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem E.1 (First-order approximation by exponential tilting). ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>. Based on Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (First-order approximation by exponential tilting). ‣ B.3 Approximating Fine-tuning Dynamics with Exponential Tilting ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, we establish that for a distribution update <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> whose KL divergence from <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding exponential-tilting approximation <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{q}_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{q}_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> differs from <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> only up to <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, exponential tilting provides a first-order approximation, thereby justifying its use as an analytical tool to study general-performance degradation and domain adaptation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs?</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we provide a theoretical explanation for the empirical findings observed in §<a href="#S3" title="3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a prefix <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> (we omit ”<math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mid u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mid u</annotation></semantics></math>” when clear).
Write <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a)=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(a)-\log q(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a)=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(a)-\log q(a)</annotation></semantics></math> at the current iterate <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> (the step index <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is omitted for readability), and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[f]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[f]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{f}=f-\bar{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{f}=f-\bar{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a set <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of token-tree nodes, denote its <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-mass by <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\mathcal{S}}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\mathcal{S}}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sparse token-level shift on <math id="A2.Thmassumption4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A2.Thmassumption4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists a measurable node set <math id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math> with small mass <math id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\mathcal{S}}\ll 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\mathcal{S}}\ll 1</annotation></semantics></math> under the <math id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-prefix distribution such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f(a)|\,\leq\,M_{h}\quad\text{for }a\in\mathcal{S},\qquad|f(a)|\,\leq\,M_{l}\quad\text{for }a\notin\mathcal{S}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.448em">≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f(a)|\,\leq\,M_{h}\quad\text{for }a\in\mathcal{S},\qquad|f(a)|\,\leq\,M_{l}\quad\text{for }a\notin\mathcal{S},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with <math id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{l}\ll M_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{l}\ll M_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In words, most tokens are already well modeled by <math id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> due to pretraining, while only a small subset requires nontrivial adjustment toward the <math id="A2.Thmassumption4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{p}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> target, denoted as the hard tokens (low probability tokens).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark.</span> This assumption reflects the practical setting where domain-specific finetuning are mainly affected by a small fraction of tokens, consistent with our empirical analysis in §<a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Token-Level Analysis ‣ 4 Token-Adaptive Loss Reweighting for Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Realizability with controlled leakage)<span id="A2.Thmassumption5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the orthogonal projections of a log-space function onto the coordinates indexed by <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and its complement, respectively (with norm measured in <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q)</annotation></semantics></math>). There exists small <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any desired log-space direction <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> (defined per-prefix on the token tree) whose energy is primarily on <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)}\leq\beta\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)}\leq\beta\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)}</annotation></semantics></math> for some small <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>), there is a parameter update that realizes a global change <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\log q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\log q</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}(\Delta\log q-g)\|_{L^{2}(q)}\leq\gamma\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)},\qquad\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\Delta\log q\|_{L^{2}(q)}\leq(\beta+\gamma)\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}(\Delta\log q-g)\|_{L^{2}(q)}\leq\gamma\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)},\qquad\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\Delta\log q\|_{L^{2}(q)}\leq(\beta+\gamma)\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(q)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In words, the update moves all tokens, but the relative magnitude outside <math id="A2.Thmassumption5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is small and controlled.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="205.73" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 205.73" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,205.73) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 199.82 C 0 203.08 2.64 205.73 5.91 205.73 L 555.16 205.73 C 558.43 205.73 561.07 203.08 561.07 199.82 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 199.82 C 1.97 202 3.73 203.76 5.91 203.76 L 555.16 203.76 C 557.34 203.76 559.1 202 559.1 199.82 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 185.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.69em;font-size:10pt;" height="185.19" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smaller steps yield a smaller general performance degradation bound at a equal domain performance gain)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix a desired domain improvement <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\star}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\star}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\leq-\Delta_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\leq-\Delta_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Among all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-step tilting schedules that achieve this target, the <em id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">minimal</em> upper bound on the increase of code length on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></span>
<span id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}\ +\ \Big(\frac{A\,C_{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}+\frac{C_{1}}{\mu_{T}^{2}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.722em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.722em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}\ +\ \Big(\frac{A\,C_{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}+\frac{C_{1}}{\mu_{T}^{2}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{T}:=\inf_{t&lt;T}\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.1389em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{T}:=\inf_{t&lt;T}\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=H_{T}\big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=H_{T}\big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed value under the total number of update steps <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and the desired domain gain <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The upper bound strictly decreases as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> increases. Thus, under the equal-steps schedule that attains the target, the per-step effective weight scales as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}\propto 1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}\propto 1/T</annotation></semantics></math>; thus, for the same domain gain, larger <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> implies smaller per-step updates. Hence, smaller step size <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> smaller upper bound.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="83.42" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 83.42" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,83.42) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 77.52 C 0 80.78 2.64 83.42 5.91 83.42 L 555.16 83.42 C 558.43 83.42 561.07 80.78 561.07 77.52 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 77.52 C 1.97 79.69 3.73 81.45 5.91 81.45 L 555.16 81.45 C 557.34 81.45 559.1 79.69 559.1 77.52 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 63.54)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:3.85em;font-size:10pt;" height="62.88" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Label-only supervision enlarges the safe per-step range)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Among all <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-step tilting schedules, the maximal per-step size that can guarantee a general-performance degradation <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\leq\varepsilon_{\rm fg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fg</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\leq\varepsilon_{\rm fg}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}=\Theta(1/{\sqrt{s}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}=\Theta(1/{\sqrt{s}})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is the expected number of hard tokens (low probability tokens) per example on <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (Smaller steps yield a smaller general performance degradation bound at a equal domain performance gain). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem B.3 (Label-only supervision enlarges the safe per-step range). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> can be found in the Appendix <a href="#A5.SS2" title="E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>. Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (Smaller steps yield a smaller general performance degradation bound at a equal domain performance gain). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> shows that, for achieving the same domain improvement, smaller learning rates (i.e., smaller per-step updates with larger <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>) lead to a smaller upper bound on general capability degradation, thereby explaining <span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Finding 1</span>. Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem B.3 (Label-only supervision enlarges the safe per-step range). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> indicates that the bound on the safe step size is inversely proportional to the number of hard tokens. Therefore, in <span id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Finding 2</span>, when only labels are used for training, the number of hard tokens is smaller than that in training with both CoT and label data. This explains why in the ESCI experiments, under w/o CoT, both <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\mathrm{e}{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\mathrm{e}{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\mathrm{e}{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\mathrm{e}{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> can achieve similarly small degradation in general performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Experiment and Result Details</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Dataset Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide additional details for both the domain-specific datasets used for SFT and the general-purpose benchmarks used to evaluate general capability degradation. An overview of all datasets and their corresponding evaluation metrics is provided in Table <a href="#A5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Table <a href="#A5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.1 </span>MedCalc</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the MedCalc dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khandekar et al., 2024</a>)</cite> for medical reasoning tasks.
The benchmark provides human-annotated chain-of-thought (CoT) rationales, which we include during training so that the model learns to reason through intermediate steps before producing the final answer. The prompt can be found in Table <a href="#A5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.2 </span>ESCI</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the ESCI dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reddy et al., 2022</a>)</cite> for a multi-class product classification task, where each query–product pair is labeled as <span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Exact</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Substitute</span>, <span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Complement</span>, or <span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Irrelevant</span>.
From the original dataset, we randomly sample a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math>K subset from the training split and a <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>K subset from the test split. From the training subset, we further hold out <math id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>K examples as a validation set.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider two training settings: <em id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/o CoT</em> and <em id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">w/ CoT</em>.</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/ CoT</span>: The target sequence includes both a chain-of-thought rationale and the final label, requiring the model to learn the reasoning process before producing the prediction. These CoT-augmented examples are generated via rejection sampling from Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct, resulting in 34,176 training examples. The prompt is shown in Table <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o CoT</span>: The target sequence contains only the ground-truth label, so the model is trained to directly predict the class without generating intermediate reasoning (49k examples). The prompt is shown in Table <a href="#A5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All prompt examples in Tables <a href="#A5.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and <a href="#A5.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> use the Qwen chat template for illustration; for other model families, we adapt the prompt to their respective chat formats.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The ESCI dataset is highly imbalanced, with the majority of samples belonging to the <span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Exact</span> category (Table <a href="#A3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ C.1.2 ESCI ‣ C.1 Dataset Details ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment and Result Details ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). This imbalance motivates our choice of <span id="A3.SS1.SSS2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">balanced accuracy</span> (BACC) as the primary evaluation metric, following prior work on imbalanced classification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Label distribution for the ESCI subsets used in our experiments. Percentages are shown in parentheses.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
