</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.3 </span>MetaMathQA</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">MetaMathQA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> is a large-scale mathematical reasoning dataset containing 395k training examples. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanyal et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we use MetaMathQA for training and take GSM8K as the target-domain evaluation benchmark. This setup allows us to validate whether our findings hold under large-scale data conditions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">C.1.4 </span>General-Purpose Benchmarks</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the general-purpose benchmarks, we fully follow the default settings and evaluation metrics implemented in the <span id="A3.SS1.SSS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lm-evaluation-harness</span> framework <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. This ensures consistency with prior work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanyal et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bansal &amp; Sanghavi, 2025</a>)</cite> and allows for fair comparison of results across different models and training configurations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We conduct all experiments on 16–32 NVIDIA A100 GPUs with 80GB memory. Except for differences in learning rate and loss computation, all experiments share the same training configuration. We adopt the AdamW optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov &amp; Hutter, 2019</a>)</cite> with hyperparameters <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>, together with a cosine annealing learning-rate schedule. The attention mechanism is implemented using FlashAttention-2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao, 2024</a>)</cite>. We set the batch size to 16 for MedCalc and ESCI, and 128 for MetaMathQA. The number of training epochs is 20 for MedCalc and ESCI, and 2 for MetaMathQA. The maximum sequence length is 8192 tokens.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Additional Details of Experimental Setup and Results</h3>

<figure id="A3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.20758v1/supp_lr_esci_gsm8k.svg" id="A3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/208;" width="548" height="208"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span><span id="A3.F4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of learning rate on domain-specific and general capability performance during supervised fine-tuning (SFT).</span> Results are shown for (a) Qwen3-8B on ESCI with CoT supervision, (b) Qwen3-8B on ESCI without CoT, and (c) DeepSeek-Coder-7B on MetaMathQA. Across all settings, smaller learning rates achieve more favorable trade-offs.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, we measure the trade-off between domain performance and general performance. Domain performance is defined as accuracy on the target downstream task, while general performance is computed as the average score across IFEval, GSM8K, and HumanEval unless otherwise specified. Importantly, our definition of general performance is consistent with the theoretical analysis, where we assume the base model already achieves reasonably strong results. To ensure consistency, we exclude benchmarks where the model’s absolute performance is below a threshold of 0.5, evaluated by <span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lm-evaluation-harness</span> framework. Thus, for Gemma-3-4B we report the average over IFEval and GSM8K, while for Gemma-3-1B we only include IFEval.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We also conduct supplementary experiments, as shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.3 Additional Details of Experimental Setup and Results ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment and Result Details ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, which further validate and extend our findings from Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Finetuning on datasets where the model already performs strongly.</span>
In Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.3 Additional Details of Experimental Setup and Results ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment and Result Details ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(a), Qwen3-8B achieves close to 50% accuracy on ESCI with CoT supervision even before SFT. Despite this high baseline, the results confirm our main conclusion: using a small learning rate continues to yield a more favorable trade-off between preserving general performance and improving domain performance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Validation on large-scale datasets.</span>
We additionally evaluate on MetaMathQA to test whether our conclusions hold under large-scale training. To emulate a realistic domain adaptation scenario, we use DeepSeek-Coder-7B, which is highly specialized in code but weaker in mathematics. This setup mirrors adapting a model from one domain of strength (code) to another (math). As shown in Figure <a href="#A3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ C.3 Additional Details of Experimental Setup and Results ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment and Result Details ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(c), we report general performance using MBPP (rather than HumanEval, since DeepSeek-Coder-7B performs poorly on HumanEval under <span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">lm-evaluation-harness</span>). The results again align with our central finding: small learning rates achieve the best trade-offs. Interestingly, in this setting the optimal rate shifts to <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, rather than <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math> as in earlier experiments. Moreover, we test an even smaller rate of <math id="A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-7}</annotation></semantics></math> and observe that <span id="A3.SS3.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">overly small rates can hinder target-domain performance</span>, suggesting that learning rates cannot be arbitrarily reduced without consequence. Overall, these additional experiments reinforce our main findings.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Effect of KL Regularization</h3>

<figure id="A3.F5" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.20758v1/kl-qwen25.svg" id="A3.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/207;" width="548" height="207"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="A3.F5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of KL regularization on domain-specific SFT.</span>
We follow DeepSeek-R1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and apply the <math id="A3.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k3</annotation></semantics></math> approximation for KL regularization.
Results are shown for three learning rates: (a) <math id="A3.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, (b) <math id="A3.F5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (c) <math id="A3.F5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Across all settings, KL regularization yields performance that is very close to standard SFT, suggesting limited additional benefit in mitigating general-performance degradation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further investigate the effect of KL regularization, a technique recently adopted in DeepSeek-R1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, where a <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k3</annotation></semantics></math> approximation is used to estimate the KL term. Following prior work on KL-constrained training <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, we add a KL penalty term with coefficient <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.001</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.001</annotation></semantics></math> during SFT.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ C.4 Effect of KL Regularization ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment and Result Details ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows results on the Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct model fine-tuned on MedCalc. At small learning rates, KL-regularized runs and standard SFT behave almost identically. As the learning rate increases, KL regularization offering little to no benefit in reducing general-performance degradation. This indicates that, under our experimental settings, KL regularization provides only limited improvements and does not shift the trade-off between domain performance and general capability preservation. These results are consistent with our earlier observation in §<a href="#S3" title="3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>: adopting a smaller learning rate already achieves a favorable balance, while additional knobs such as KL regularization contribute little further advantage.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.5 </span>Evaluation on Multi-Choice Commonsense and Knowledge QA</h3>

<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.20758v1/multi-choice.svg" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/146;" width="548" height="146"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span><span id="A3.F6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of learning rate on the trade-off between domain performance and general multi-choice commonsense and knowledge QA performance.</span> Domain performance is measured on MedCalc, while general performance is evaluated as the average accuracy across MMLU, ARC-Easy, ARC-Challenge, PIQA, and HellaSwag. Results are shown for (a) Qwen3-8B, (b) Qwen2.5-7B, (c) Qwen3-4B, and (d) Qwen2.5-3B.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We further evaluate the effect of learning rate on the trade-off between domain and general performance in multi-choice commonsense and knowledge question answering tasks. Results are presented in Figure <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ C.5 Evaluation on Multi-Choice Commonsense and Knowledge QA ‣ Appendix C Additional Experiment and Result Details ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Unlike our earlier observations on more complex domains such as mathematics and coding, we find that the general-performance degradation induced by relatively larger learning rates (e.g., <math id="A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\mathrm{e}{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\mathrm{e}{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>) is less pronounced here. A possible explanation is that multi-choice benchmarks are relatively more trivial, requiring short-form predictions rather than long reasoning chains or structured outputs. As a result, larger learning rates do not amplify forgetting as severely as in domains demanding longer and more complex generations.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Details of Token-Adaptive Loss Reweighting</h2>

<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm">
<div id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.3.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Domain dataset <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, parameters <math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>, temperature <math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, weight floor <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>Updated parameters <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.3" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.3.3.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">training step</em> <span id="algorithm1.3.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Sample a mini-batch <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x^{(b)}_{\text{prompt}},y^{(b)})\}_{b=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mtext>prompt</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x^{(b)}_{\text{prompt}},y^{(b)})\}_{b=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Forward pass to obtain token probabilities <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for all supervised tokens in the batch;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> Token NLLs: <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{t}\leftarrow-\log p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{t}\leftarrow-\log p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive weights with lower-bound clipping:</span>

<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{w}_{t}\leftarrow\exp(-\ell_{t}/\tau),\qquad w_{t}\leftarrow\max\!\big(\operatorname{sg}(\tilde{w}_{t}),\,w_{\min}\big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>sg</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{w}_{t}\leftarrow\exp(-\ell_{t}/\tau),\qquad w_{t}\leftarrow\max\!\big(\operatorname{sg}(\tilde{w}_{t}),\,w_{\min}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>Let <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of supervised tokens in the batch;
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.3.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mean (averaged) reweighted loss:</span>

<table id="A4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{TALR}}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{t=1}^{N}w_{t}\,(-\log p_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>TALR</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{TALR}}\;=\;\frac{1}{N}\sum_{t=1}^{N}w_{t}\,(-\log p_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>Parameter update:

<table id="A4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\leftarrow\theta\;-\;\eta\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{TALR}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>TALR</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\leftarrow\theta\;-\;\eta\,\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\text{TALR}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.9" class="ltx_listingline">end foreach
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.3.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:397.5pt;height:1.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>

</div>
</div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Token-Adaptive Loss Reweighting (TALR) for Domain-Specific SFT. The <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{sg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{sg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> operator denotes <em id="algorithm1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">stop gradient</em>, meaning that <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as a constant during backpropagation to prevent gradients from flowing through the weight computation.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Deriving Token Weights: Proof of the Closed-form Solution</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Introduce a Lagrange multiplier <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the simplex constraint <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}w_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}w_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and multipliers <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for the nonnegativity constraints. The Lagrangian is</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{w},\lambda,\bm{\mu})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big(w_{i}\ell_{i}(\theta)+\tau w_{i}\log w_{i}\Big)+\lambda\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}-1\Big)-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mu_{i}w_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐰</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\mathbf{w},\lambda,\bm{\mu})=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Big(w_{i}\ell_{i}(\theta)+\tau w_{i}\log w_{i}\Big)+\lambda\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{n}w_{i}-1\Big)-\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mu_{i}w_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">For an interior optimum (<math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>), the KKT condition is</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{i}}=\ell_{i}(\theta)+\tau(1+\log w_{i})+\lambda=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial w_{i}}=\ell_{i}(\theta)+\tau(1+\log w_{i})+\lambda=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log w_{i}=-\frac{\ell_{i}(\theta)+\lambda}{\tau}-1\quad\Longrightarrow\quad w_{i}=\exp\!\Big(-\tfrac{\ell_{i}(\theta)}{\tau}\Big)\cdot\exp\!\Big(-\tfrac{\lambda}{\tau}-1\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log w_{i}=-\frac{\ell_{i}(\theta)+\lambda}{\tau}-1\quad\Longrightarrow\quad w_{i}=\exp\!\Big(-\tfrac{\ell_{i}(\theta)}{\tau}\Big)\cdot\exp\!\Big(-\tfrac{\lambda}{\tau}-1\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Normalization by <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}w_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}w_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{n}\exp\!\Big(-\tfrac{\ell_{j}(\theta)}{\tau}\Big),\qquad w_{i}^{*}\;=\;\frac{\exp\!\big(-\ell_{i}(\theta)/\tau\big)}{Z}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\;=\;\sum_{j=1}^{n}\exp\!\Big(-\tfrac{\ell_{j}(\theta)}{\tau}\Big),\qquad w_{i}^{*}\;=\;\frac{\exp\!\big(-\ell_{i}(\theta)/\tau\big)}{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Implementation Details of TALR</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We highlight two key design considerations in applying TALR.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Weight cutoff.</span> Without constraints, hard tokens may receive extremely small weights, which slows down learning or even prevents the model from learning these tokens. To address this, we introduce a lower bound cutoff to ensure that no token weight becomes too small. In all our experiments, we set this cutoff to <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, which strikes a balance between preventing vanishing weights and still allowing TALR to downweight challenging tokens.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Choice of <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> The temperature <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> controls the sharpness of weight assignment and is a crucial hyperparameter. In our experiments, <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is chosen dynamically as the median of the average sequence loss within a batch, a strategy that consistently yields stable and strong performance across tasks. To better illustrate the effect of <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, we plot Figure <a href="#A4.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ D.2 Implementation Details of TALR ‣ Appendix D Details of Token-Adaptive Loss Reweighting ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. When a batch contains more hard tokens, the resulting <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is larger; in this case, weights assigned to hard tokens are not excessively small, preventing the model from failing to learn. Conversely, when the overall loss is smaller, the resulting <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> decreases, which effectively acts as a hard clipping mechanism to prevent excessive parameter drift and catastrophic forgetting. Nonetheless, the problem of selecting <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> remains open, and future work may explore more principled or adaptive strategies for temperature tuning in TALR.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.20758v1/tau_effect.svg" id="A4.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:274/201;" width="274" height="201"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><span id="A4.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of the temperature parameter <math id="A4.F7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> on the token weighting function <math id="A4.F7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}=p^{1/\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}=p^{1/\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> Smaller <math id="A4.F7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> values (e.g., <math id="A4.F7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.F7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>) sharply down-weight low-probability (hard) tokens, leading to a steep weighting curve. Larger <math id="A4.F7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> values (e.g., <math id="A4.F7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=2,5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=2,5</annotation></semantics></math>) flatten the curve, assigning relatively higher weights to hard tokens. The case <math id="A4.F7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the identity mapping. This illustrates how <math id="A4.F7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> modulates the balance between emphasizing easy versus hard tokens.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>More Discussions</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Comparison with FLOW.</span>
It is worth contrasting TALR with FLOW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sanyal et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, which also reweights losses but in a different manner. First, FLOW operates at the <em id="A4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sequence level</em>, whereas TALR works at the <em id="A4.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">token level</em>. Second, FLOW computes static weights only once before training, while TALR dynamically updates weights at every batch with negligible additional cost. As shown in Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.2 Results ‣ 4 Token-Adaptive Loss Reweighting for Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, TALR consistently outperforms FLOW, which aligns with our expectations. Sequence-level loss can be misleading: for example, even when the overall average sequence loss is small, there may exist a few particularly hard tokens with large losses that are overlooked at the sequence granularity. TALR directly addresses this by reweighting at the token level. Moreover, token difficulty is not fixed—its relative hardness evolves as training progresses, as discussed in Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Token-Level Analysis ‣ 4 Token-Adaptive Loss Reweighting for Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>. This makes dynamic weighting naturally more advantageous than static approaches.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Why not fix <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
We also examine the impact of fixing the temperature parameter, e.g., setting <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the weights of hard tokens become excessively small, which severely hampers the model’s ability to learn from them. Empirically, we observe that such a fixed choice indeed leads to poor results. For example, on Qwen3-4B fine-tuned with MedCalc at a learning rate of <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>, fixing <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math> yields a maximum accuracy of only <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.2168" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.2168</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.2168</annotation></semantics></math>, much lower than results in Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 3.2 Main Results ‣ 3 Learning Rate Matters: Revisiting Its Role in General Capability Degradation during Domain-Specific SFT ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. This stark degradation confirms that without dynamic adjustment, the model fails to effectively learn from hard tokens. By contrast, our dynamic strategy for selecting <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., based on the median of average sequence losses in each batch, automatically adapts to the current distribution of token difficulties, ensuring that hard tokens are downweighted without being entirely neglected.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (First-order approximation by exponential tilting). ‣ B.3 Approximating Fine-tuning Dynamics with Exponential Tilting ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="140.88" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 140.88" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,140.88) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 134.97 C 0 138.23 2.64 140.88 5.91 140.88 L 555.16 140.88 C 558.43 140.88 561.07 138.23 561.07 134.97 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 134.97 C 1.97 137.14 3.73 138.91 5.91 138.91 L 555.16 138.91 C 557.34 138.91 559.1 137.14 559.1 134.97 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 120.92)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.7em;--ltx-fo-depth:8em;font-size:10pt;" height="120.34" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.69)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First-order approximation by exponential tilting)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix a prefix <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>. Consider the current model distribution <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math> and the smoothed target distribution <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the local <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|g\|_{t,u}:=\big(\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)}[g(a)^{2}]\big)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.0835em" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g\|_{t,u}:=\big(\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)}[g(a)^{2}]\big)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the standing assumptions, there exists an effective step size <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t,u}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Big\|\log q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)-\Big[(1-\lambda_{t,u})\,\log q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)+\lambda_{t,u}\,\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)-\psi_{t,u}\Big]\Big\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.0835em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big\|\log q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)-\Big[(1-\lambda_{t,u})\,\log q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)+\lambda_{t,u}\,\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)-\psi_{t,u}\Big]\Big\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t,u}</annotation></semantics></math> is the log-normalizer and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is the KL trust-region radius such that <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)\ \leq\ \varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)\ \leq\ \varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a prefix <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math>.
For clarity we write <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot)=q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot)=q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t+1}(\cdot)=q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t+1}(\cdot)=q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A5.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot)=\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot)=\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1. Log-shift representation of the true update.</span>
Define the centered log-shift</p>
<table id="A5.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(a)\ :=\ \log\frac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(a)\ :=\ \log\frac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then, we have</p>
<table id="A5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q_{t+1}(a)\ =\ \frac{q_{t}(a)\,e^{s(a)}}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{s}]}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>s</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q_{t+1}(a)\ =\ \frac{q_{t}(a)\,e^{s(a)}}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{s}]}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2. Log-shift representation of exponential tilting.</span>
For any <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, define</p>
<table id="A5.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)\ =\ \frac{q_{t}(a)\,\exp\{\lambda r(a)\}}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{\lambda r}]},\qquad r(a):=\log\frac{\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)\ =\ \frac{q_{t}(a)\,\exp\{\lambda r(a)\}}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{\lambda r}]},\qquad r(a):=\log\frac{\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3. Size of the true log-shift (forward KL trust region).</span>
Write <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t}(\cdot)=q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}(\cdot)=q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{t+1}(\cdot)=q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t+1}(\cdot)=q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recall the centered log-shift</p>
<table id="A5.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(a)\ :=\ \log\frac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}\;-\;\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\right],\qquad\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}\ :=\ \mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(a)\ :=\ \log\frac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}\;-\;\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\right],\qquad\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}\ :=\ \mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Let the log-partition <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(f):=\log\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{f}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(f):=\log\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{f}]</annotation></semantics></math> and the exponential-family map</p>
<table id="A5.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T(f)(a)\ :=\ \frac{q_{t}(a)e^{f(a)}}{e^{A(f)}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T(f)(a)\ :=\ \frac{q_{t}(a)e^{f(a)}}{e^{A(f)}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t+1}=T(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t+1}=T(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A5.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{q_{t}}{q_{t+1}}\right]=A(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{q_{t}}{q_{t+1}}\right]=A(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.4" class="ltx_p">Two standard identities (for discrete finite support) are</p>
<table id="A5.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla A(f)[h]=\mathbb{E}_{T(f)}[h],\qquad\nabla^{2}A(f)[h,k]=\mathrm{Cov}_{T(f)}(h,k)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Cov</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla A(f)[h]=\mathbb{E}_{T(f)}[h],\qquad\nabla^{2}A(f)[h,k]=\mathrm{Cov}_{T(f)}(h,k).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is centered under <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla A(0)[s]=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla A(0)[s]=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s]=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
A second-order Taylor expansion of <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> with a third-order remainder yields</p>
<table id="A5.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(s)=A(0)+\nabla A(0)[s]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\nabla^{2}A(0)[s,s]+R_{3}(s)=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(s)+R_{3}(s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(s)=A(0)+\nabla A(0)[s]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\nabla^{2}A(0)[s,s]+R_{3}(s)=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(s)+R_{3}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.6" class="ltx_p">where, because the vocabulary is finite and <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> has full support (by smoothing), there exists a constant <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|R_{3}(s)|\;\leq\;C_{3}\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|R_{3}(s)|\;\leq\;C_{3}\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.7" class="ltx_p">Combining equation <a href="#A5.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>–equation <a href="#A5.E5" title="In Proof. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> gives the quadratic expansion</p>
<table id="A5.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}+O\!\big(\|s\|_{t,u}^{3}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>s</mi><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}\!\big(q_{t}\,\|\,q_{t+1}\big)=\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}+O\!\big(\|s\|_{t,u}^{3}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.8" class="ltx_p">Finally, under the trust-region assumption <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m13" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(q_{t}\|q_{t+1})\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(q_{t}\|q_{t+1})\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and
for <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s\|_{t,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s\|_{t,u}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small, there exists a constant <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}-C\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{3}\;\leq\;\varepsilon," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}-C\,\|s\|_{t,u}^{3}\;\leq\;\varepsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.9" class="ltx_p">which implies <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s\|_{t,u}\leq 4\sqrt{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s\|_{t,u}\leq 4\sqrt{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> as soon as
<math id="A5.SS1.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s\|_{t,u}\leq\min\{1/(4C),1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s\|_{t,u}\leq\min\{1/(4C),1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s\|_{t,u}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s\|_{t,u}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4. First-order expansion of tilting.</span>
Recall the tilted distribution</p>
<table id="A5.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\frac{q_{t}(a)\,e^{\lambda r(a)}}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{\lambda r}]},\qquad r(a)=\log\frac{\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)}{q_{t}(a\mid u)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\frac{q_{t}(a)\,e^{\lambda r(a)}}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{\lambda r}]},\qquad r(a)=\log\frac{\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a\mid u)}{q_{t}(a\mid u)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Its log-ratio relative to <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}=\lambda\,r(a)-A(\lambda r),\qquad A(f):=\log\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{f}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}=\lambda\,r(a)-A(\lambda r),\qquad A(f):=\log\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{f}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Taylor expansion of <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\lambda r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\lambda r)</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>, using
<math id="A5.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla A(0)[r]=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla A(0)[r]=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A5.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla^{2}A(0)[r,r]=\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo>∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla^{2}A(0)[r,r]=\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\lambda r)=\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+\tfrac{1}{6}\,\lambda^{3}\,\kappa_{3}(r)+O(\lambda^{4})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\lambda r)=\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]+\tfrac{1}{2}\,\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+\tfrac{1}{6}\,\lambda^{3}\,\kappa_{3}(r)+O(\lambda^{4}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa_{3}(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa_{3}(r)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the third central moment of <math id="A5.SS1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> (bounded on finite support).
Hence</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}=\lambda\big(r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]\big)-\tfrac{1}{2}\,\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}=\lambda\big(r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]\big)-\tfrac{1}{2}\,\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now consider the centered log-shift</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a):=\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a):=\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\right]=\lambda\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]-A(\lambda r)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\,\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\lambda^{3})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\left[\log\frac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\right]=\lambda\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]-A(\lambda r)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\,\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\lambda^{3}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">the quadratic terms cancel, yielding</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\lambda\big(r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]\big)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\lambda\big(r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]\big)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 5. Choice of effective step size.</span>
Let <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}(a):=r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}(a):=r(a)-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]</annotation></semantics></math> be the centered tilting direction and recall from Step 4 that the centered log-shift of the tilted model satisfies</p>
<table id="A5.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\lambda\,r_{c}(a)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\lambda\,r_{c}(a)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Define the effective step size by <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>-least-squares matching:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t,u}:=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[s\,r_{c}\big]}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[r_{c}^{2}\big]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t,u}:=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[s\,r_{c}\big]}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[r_{c}^{2}\big]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p">By Cauchy–Schwarz,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{t,u}|=\frac{|\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s\,r_{c}]|}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]}\leq\frac{\|s\|_{t,u}\,\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}}{\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}^{2}}=\frac{\|s\|_{t,u}}{\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{t,u}|=\frac{|\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s\,r_{c}]|}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]}\leq\frac{\|s\|_{t,u}\,\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}}{\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}^{2}}=\frac{\|s\|_{t,u}}{\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p9.4" class="ltx_p">Since Step 3 gives <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s\|_{t,u}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s\|_{t,u}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> and we assume <math id="A5.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]\geq v_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}^{2}=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]\geq v_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> (non-degenerate target),
it follows that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{t,u}|=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{t,u}|=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next we control the residual.
Under the smoothness and small-step assumptions, the true shift <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> and the tilting direction <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> agree to first order:
there exists a scalar <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> and a remainder <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\alpha\,r_{c}+\Delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\alpha\,r_{c}+\Delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into the formula for <math id="A5.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t,u}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t,u}=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[(\alpha r_{c}+\Delta)r_{c}]}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]}=\alpha+\frac{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[\Delta\,r_{c}]}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]}=\alpha+O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t,u}=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[(\alpha r_{c}+\Delta)r_{c}]}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]}=\alpha+\frac{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[\Delta\,r_{c}]}{\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r_{c}^{2}]}=\alpha+O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence the residual can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}=\Delta-(\lambda_{t,u}-\alpha)r_{c}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}=\Delta-(\lambda_{t,u}-\alpha)r_{c},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\,s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\,\|_{t,u}\leq\|\Delta\|_{t,u}+|\lambda_{t,u}-\alpha|\,\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\,s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\,\|_{t,u}\leq\|\Delta\|_{t,u}+|\lambda_{t,u}-\alpha|\,\|r_{c}\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 6. Putting pieces together.</span>
Recall that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=(1-\lambda)\log q_{t}(a)+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a)-\psi_{t,u}(\lambda)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=(1-\lambda)\log q_{t}(a)+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a)-\psi_{t,u}(\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p">so that the log-difference vector is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(\lambda)}(a):=\log q_{t+1}(a)-\log\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\Big(\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\big]\Big)-\Big(\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\big]\Big)+C(\lambda)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(\lambda)}(a):=\log q_{t+1}(a)-\log\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=\Big(\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\big]\Big)-\Big(\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\big]\Big)+C(\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p11.3" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A5.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\lambda)\ :=\ \mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\Big]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\lambda)\ :=\ \mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\Big]-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p11.4" class="ltx_p">is a constant (independent of <math id="A5.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>). Denote</p>
<table id="A5.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(a):=\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\big],\qquad\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a):=\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(a):=\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\big],\qquad\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}(a):=\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)}{q_{t}(a)}-\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p11.5" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A5.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{(\lambda)}(a)=\big(s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\big)(a)+C(\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{(\lambda)}(a)=\big(s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\big)(a)+C(\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s]=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[s]=\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}]=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the vector <math id="A5.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math>
is orthogonal (in <math id="A5.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(q_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(q_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>) to the constant function <math id="A5.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta^{(\lambda)}\|_{t,u}^{2}=\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\,\|_{t,u}^{2}+|C(\lambda)|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta^{(\lambda)}\|_{t,u}^{2}=\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\,\|_{t,u}^{2}+|C(\lambda)|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">and in particular</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\,\|_{t,u}\ \leq\ \|\Delta^{(\lambda)}\|_{t,u}\ \leq\ \|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\,\|_{t,u}+|C(\lambda)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\,\|_{t,u}\ \leq\ \|\Delta^{(\lambda)}\|_{t,u}\ \leq\ \|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}\,\|_{t,u}+|C(\lambda)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(f):=\log\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{f}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>f</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(f):=\log\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[e^{f}]</annotation></semantics></math> and Eq. <a href="#A5.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Using</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\Big]=-A(s),\qquad\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\Big]=\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]-A(\lambda r)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{q_{t+1}}{q_{t}}\Big]=-A(s),\qquad\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}\!\Big[\log\tfrac{\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}}{q_{t}}\Big]=\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]-A(\lambda r),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\lambda)=-A(s)-\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]+A(\lambda r)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\lambda)=-A(s)-\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]+A(\lambda r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">By Step 3, <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(s)=\tfrac{1}{2}\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}+O(\|s\|_{t,u}^{3})=O(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(s)=\tfrac{1}{2}\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}+O(\|s\|_{t,u}^{3})=O(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the Taylor expansion of <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\lambda r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\lambda r)</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> (Step 4),</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\lambda r)=\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]+\tfrac{1}{2}\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\lambda r)=\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{q_{t}}[r]+\tfrac{1}{2}\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p13.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p13.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\lambda)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\|s\|_{t,u}^{3})+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\lambda)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\|s\|_{t,u}^{2}+\tfrac{1}{2}\lambda^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{q_{t}}(r)+O(\|s\|_{t,u}^{3})+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p13.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p13.5.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, with <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda|=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda|=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> (Step 5) and <math id="A5.SS1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|s\|_{t,u}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>ε</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|s\|_{t,u}=O(\sqrt{\varepsilon})</annotation></semantics></math> (Step 3),</span></p>
<table id="A5.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|C(\lambda)|=O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|C(\lambda)|=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=\lambda_{t,u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=\lambda_{t,u}</annotation></semantics></math> from Step 5. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\,\|_{t,u}\leq\|\,s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\,\|_{t,u}+\|\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\|_{t,u}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\,\|_{t,u}\leq\|\,s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\,\|_{t,u}+\|\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\|_{t,u}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Step 5, <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\,s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\,\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\,s-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\,\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.
By Step 4, <math id="A5.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}=\lambda r_{c}+O(\lambda^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}^{(\lambda)}=\lambda r_{c}+O(\lambda^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="A5.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\|_{t,u}=O(\lambda_{t,u}^{3})=O(\varepsilon^{3/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}-\lambda_{t,u}r_{c}\|_{t,u}=O(\lambda_{t,u}^{3})=O(\varepsilon^{3/2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\,\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\,\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using the decomposition inequality above and equation <a href="#A5.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ E.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Delta^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\|_{t,u}\leq\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\,\|_{t,u}+|C(\lambda_{t,u})|=O(\varepsilon)+O(\varepsilon)=O(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Delta^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\|_{t,u}\leq\|\,s-\tilde{s}^{(\lambda_{t,u})}\,\|_{t,u}+|C(\lambda_{t,u})|=O(\varepsilon)+O(\varepsilon)=O(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, recalling</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=(1-\lambda)\log q_{t}(a)+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a)-\psi_{t,u}(\lambda)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\widehat{q}^{(\lambda)}(a)=(1-\lambda)\log q_{t}(a)+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(a)-\psi_{t,u}(\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p14.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p14.5.1" class="ltx_text">we have shown</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Big\|\log q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)-\Big[(1-\lambda_{t,u})\,\log q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)+\lambda_{t,u}\,\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)-\psi_{t,u}(\lambda_{t,u})\Big]\Big\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big\|\log q_{t+1}(\cdot\mid u)-\Big[(1-\lambda_{t,u})\,\log q_{t}(\cdot\mid u)+\lambda_{t,u}\,\log\tilde{p}_{2,t}(\cdot\mid u)-\psi_{t,u}(\lambda_{t,u})\Big]\Big\|_{t,u}=O(\varepsilon),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">which proves the theorem.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem B.2 (Smaller steps yield a smaller general performance degradation bound at a equal domain performance gain). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a></h3>

<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a prefix <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> (we omit ”<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mid u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mid u</annotation></semantics></math>” when clear).
Write <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a)=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(a)-\log q(a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a)=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(a)-\log q(a)</annotation></semantics></math> at the current iterate <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> (the step index <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is omitted for readability), and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[f]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[f]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{f}=f-\bar{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{f}=f-\bar{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For a set <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> of token-tree nodes, denote its <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-mass by <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\mathcal{S}}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\mathcal{S}}=\mathbb{E}_{q}[\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Recall the standard log-space interpolation <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> defined per prefix by
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q_{\lambda}=(1-\lambda)\log q+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2}-\psi(\lambda)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q_{\lambda}=(1-\lambda)\log q+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2}-\psi(\lambda),</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\psi(\lambda)=\log\sum_{a}q(a)^{1-\lambda}\tilde{p}_{2}(a)^{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\lambda)=\log\sum_{a}q(a)^{1-\lambda}\tilde{p}_{2}(a)^{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(First-order change of code length under tilting)<span id="A5.Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any response distribution <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> on the token tree,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P):=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)=-\,\lambda\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\Big)\ +\ O(\lambda^{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P):=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)=-\,\lambda\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\Big)\ +\ O(\lambda^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\lambda^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\lambda^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> remainder is controlled by <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Equivalently,
<math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{d}{d\lambda}\big|_{\lambda=0}\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})=-\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{d\lambda}\big|_{\lambda=0}\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})=-\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big).</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q_{\lambda}=\log q+\lambda(f-\psi(\lambda))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q_{\lambda}=\log q+\lambda(f-\psi(\lambda))</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\lambda)=\log\mathbb{E}_{Q}[e^{\lambda f}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\lambda)=\log\mathbb{E}_{Q}[e^{\lambda f}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{q_{\lambda}}{q}=\lambda f-\psi(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mi>q</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{q_{\lambda}}{q}=\lambda f-\psi(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)-\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]+\psi(\lambda)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)-\lambda\,\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]+\psi(\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\lambda)=\log\mathbb{E}_{Q}[e^{\lambda f}]=\lambda\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\lambda)=\log\mathbb{E}_{Q}[e^{\lambda f}]=\lambda\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})</annotation></semantics></math>,
we obtain
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(P)=-\lambda(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f])+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P)=-\lambda(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f])+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Variance under sparsity)<span id="A5.Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix a prefix <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Q(\cdot)=q(\cdot\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\cdot)=q(\cdot\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(a)=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(a\mid u)-\log q(a\mid u)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(a)=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(a\mid u)-\log q(a\mid u)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmassumption4" title="Assumption B.4 (Sparse token-level shift on 𝒟_2). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{a\sim Q}[f(a)^{2}]\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ (1-w_{\mathcal{S}})\,M_{l}^{2}\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ M_{l}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{a\sim Q}[f(a)^{2}]\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ (1-w_{\mathcal{S}})\,M_{l}^{2}\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ M_{l}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Moreover, when we account for the controlled leakage in Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmassumption5" title="Assumption B.5 (Realizability with controlled leakage). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>,
the <em id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">effective</em> out-of-set amplitude can be taken as
<math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h},</annotation></semantics></math>
which yields the coarse bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ \big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>eff</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ \big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)\leq\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)\leq\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, it suffices to bound the second moment.
Split the expectation over <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f^{2}]=\mathbb{E}_{Q}\!\big[f^{2}\,\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}}\big]+\mathbb{E}_{Q}\!\big[f^{2}\,\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\big]\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}M_{h}^{2}+(1-w_{\mathcal{S}})M_{l}^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f^{2}]=\mathbb{E}_{Q}\!\big[f^{2}\,\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}}\big]+\mathbb{E}_{Q}\!\big[f^{2}\,\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\big]\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}M_{h}^{2}+(1-w_{\mathcal{S}})M_{l}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">using <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f|\leq M_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f|\leq M_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f|\leq M_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f|\leq M_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Dropping the factor <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-w_{\mathcal{S}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-w_{\mathcal{S}})</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq w_{\mathcal{S}}M_{h}^{2}+M_{l}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq w_{\mathcal{S}}M_{h}^{2}+M_{l}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">To upper bound the <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">effective</em> out-of-set magnitude after realizing a targeted update on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose the per-prefix target direction</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:=\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}f," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:=\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}f,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is supported on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}=0\leq\beta\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}=0\leq\beta\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}</annotation></semantics></math>
and the premise of Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmassumption5" title="Assumption B.5 (Realizability with controlled leakage). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> holds.
Let <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\log q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\log q</annotation></semantics></math> be the induced global change guaranteed by Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmassumption5" title="Assumption B.5 (Realizability with controlled leakage). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>, and define the <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">leakage vector</em> on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}^{c}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell:=\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\,\Delta\log q." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell:=\Pi_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\,\Delta\log q.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Then the out-of-set control in Assumption <a href="#A2.Thmassumption5" title="Assumption B.5 (Realizability with controlled leakage). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.4 Why Smaller Learning Rates Yield Favorable Trade-offs? ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Analysis ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\ell\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq(\beta+\gamma)\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\ell\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq(\beta+\gamma)\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}=\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}f\|_{L^{2}(Q)}=\Big(\mathbb{E}_{a\sim Q}\big[(\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}f(a))^{2}\big]\Big)^{1/2}\leq M_{h}\,\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\leq M_{h}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}=\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}f\|_{L^{2}(Q)}=\Big(\mathbb{E}_{a\sim Q}\big[(\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}f(a))^{2}\big]\Big)^{1/2}\leq M_{h}\,\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\leq M_{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define the <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">effective</em> out-of-set component that accounts for leakage by</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\mathrm{eff}}_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}:=f_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}+\ell." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mi>eff</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\mathrm{eff}}_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}:=f_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}+\ell.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">By the triangle inequality and the bounds above,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f^{\mathrm{eff}}_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq\|f_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}+\|\ell\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)\,M_{h}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><mi>eff</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f^{\mathrm{eff}}_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq\|f_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}+\|\ell\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)\,\|\Pi_{\mathcal{S}}g\|_{L^{2}(Q)}\leq M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)\,M_{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, an effective second-moment upper bound that incorporates the controlled leakage is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f^{2}]=\|f_{\mathcal{S}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}^{2}+\|f_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}^{2}\leq w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}+\big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f^{2}]=\|f_{\mathcal{S}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}^{2}+\|f_{\mathcal{S}^{c}}\|_{L^{2}(Q)}^{2}\leq w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}+\big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">This motivates the shorthand</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}+\big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>eff</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}+\big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">which we use as a coarse variance upper bound when controlled leakage is present.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P,Q,\tilde{P}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P,Q,\tilde{P}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be response distributions on the (truncated) token space with strictly positive densities <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p,q,\tilde{p}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p,q,\tilde{p}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z):=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\log q(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z):=\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\log q(z)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|\tilde{P}_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|\tilde{P}_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> then
<math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|P_{2})\geq 0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|P_{2})\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Expand the left-hand side:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{z}p(z)\,\big(\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\log q(z)\big)-\sum_{z}q(z)\,\big(\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\log q(z)\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{z}p(z)\,\big(\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\log q(z)\big)-\sum_{z}q(z)\,\big(\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\log q(z)\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Group like terms:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Big(\sum_{z}p(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\sum_{z}p(z)\log q(z)\Big)-\Big(\sum_{z}q(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\sum_{z}q(z)\log q(z)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Big(\sum_{z}p(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\sum_{z}p(z)\log q(z)\Big)-\Big(\sum_{z}q(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)-\sum_{z}q(z)\log q(z)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Use the discrete KL definitions:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)=\sum_{z}p(z)\log\frac{p(z)}{q(z)}=\sum_{z}p(z)\log p(z)-\sum_{z}p(z)\log q(z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)=\sum_{z}p(z)\log\frac{p(z)}{q(z)}=\sum_{z}p(z)\log p(z)-\sum_{z}p(z)\log q(z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A5.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})=\sum_{z}q(z)\log\frac{q(z)}{\tilde{p}_{2}(z)}=\sum_{z}q(z)\log q(z)-\sum_{z}q(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})=\sum_{z}q(z)\log\frac{q(z)}{\tilde{p}_{2}(z)}=\sum_{z}q(z)\log q(z)-\sum_{z}q(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A5.Ex71" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P\|\tilde{P}_{2})=\sum_{z}p(z)\log\frac{p(z)}{\tilde{p}_{2}(z)}=\sum_{z}p(z)\log p(z)-\sum_{z}p(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P\|\tilde{P}_{2})=\sum_{z}p(z)\log\frac{p(z)}{\tilde{p}_{2}(z)}=\sum_{z}p(z)\log p(z)-\sum_{z}p(z)\log\tilde{p}_{2}(z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute and simplify to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{z}p(z)f(z)-\sum_{z}q(z)f(z)=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|\tilde{P}_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>z</mi></munder><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{z}p(z)f(z)-\sum_{z}q(z)f(z)=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|\tilde{P}_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the right-hand side equals
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|P_{2})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\|P_{2})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,
with equality iff <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We now bound the domain performance improvement and the general capability degradation in a single small step.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="309.35" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 309.35" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,309.35) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 303.45 C 0 306.71 2.64 309.35 5.91 309.35 L 555.16 309.35 C 558.43 309.35 561.07 306.71 561.07 303.45 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 303.45 C 1.97 305.62 3.73 307.38 5.91 307.38 L 555.16 307.38 C 557.34 307.38 559.1 305.62 559.1 303.45 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 289.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:20.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="288.81" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p10.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step code-length change bounds)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{1},P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{1},P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> be the response distributions of <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1},\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1},\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> on the truncated token tree, and let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q\mapsto Q_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q\mapsto Q_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> be one log-space tilting step with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda|\leq\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda|\leq\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> small. Denote the expected code-length change by <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P):=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P):=\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{\lambda})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then there exist constants <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Domain performance improvement on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A5.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A5.Ex73"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta L(P_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta L(P_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\,\lambda\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\Big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Var</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\,\lambda\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\Big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex74"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\,\lambda\Big(\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|\tilde{P}_{2})\Big)+C_{2}\,\lambda^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\,\lambda\Big(\mathrm{KL}(Q\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|\tilde{P}_{2})\Big)+C_{2}\,\lambda^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">General performance degradation on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A5.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A5.Ex75"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta L(P_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta L(P_{1})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\,\lambda\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\Big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Var</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\,\lambda\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\Big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex76"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\lambda\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}\,\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Var</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\lambda\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}\,\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex77"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\lambda\Big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\Big)\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\lambda\Big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\Big)\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">χ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the chi-square divergence.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In particular, if <math id="A5.Thmtheorem2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P_{2})\ \leq\ -\,\lambda\,\mathrm{KL}(Q\|P_{2})\ +\ C_{2}\,\lambda^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P_{2})\ \leq\ -\,\lambda\,\mathrm{KL}(Q\|P_{2})\ +\ C_{2}\,\lambda^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the definition of the one-step log-space interpolation (per prefix)
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log q_{\lambda}=(1-\lambda)\log q+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2}-\psi(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log q_{\lambda}=(1-\lambda)\log q+\lambda\log\tilde{p}_{2}-\psi(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>,
with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(\lambda)=\log\mathbb{E}_{Q}[e^{\lambda f}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(\lambda)=\log\mathbb{E}_{Q}[e^{\lambda f}]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\log\tilde{p}_{2}-\log q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\log\tilde{p}_{2}-\log q</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any distribution <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> on responses, Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma E.1 (First-order change of code length under tilting). ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> gives the second-order expansion</span></p>
<table id="A5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P):=\mathrm{KL}(P\!\parallel\!Q_{\lambda})-\mathrm{KL}(P\!\parallel\!Q)=-\,\lambda\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.611em;" width="0.611em"><mi>P</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.611em;" width="0.611em"><mi>P</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P):=\mathrm{KL}(P\!\parallel\!Q_{\lambda})-\mathrm{KL}(P\!\parallel\!Q)=-\,\lambda\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Domain performance improvement on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Apply equation <a href="#A5.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(P_{2})=-\,\lambda\big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P_{2})=-\,\lambda\big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>Q</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>Q</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Multiplying by <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> reverses the inequality, hence for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda|\leq\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda|\leq\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P_{2})\leq-\,\lambda\Big(\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})\Big)+C_{2}\,\lambda^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>Q</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P_{2})\leq-\,\lambda\Big(\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!\tilde{P}_{2})\Big)+C_{2}\,\lambda^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, when <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!P_{2})\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!P_{2})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>Q</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>Q</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\!\parallel\!Q)+\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!P_{2})\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!P_{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">so</p>
<table id="A5.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L(P_{2})\leq-\,\lambda\,\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!P_{2})+C_{2}\,\lambda^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>Q</mi></mpadded><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo>∥</mo></mpadded><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P_{2})\leq-\,\lambda\,\mathrm{KL}(Q\!\parallel\!P_{2})+C_{2}\,\lambda^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">General performance degradation on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Apply equation <a href="#A5.E8" title="In Proof. ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(P_{1})=-\,\lambda\big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P_{1})=-\,\lambda\big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)+O(\lambda^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Using the inequality <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathbb{E}_{P}[g]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[g]|\leq\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(g)}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P\|Q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbb{E}_{P}[g]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[g]|\leq\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(g)}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P\|Q)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big|\leq\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\!\parallel\!Q)}\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f]-\mathbb{E}_{Q}[f]\big|\leq\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\!\parallel\!Q)}\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda|\leq\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda|\leq\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(P_{1})\leq\lambda\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}\,\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\!\parallel\!Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P_{1})\leq\lambda\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}\,\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\!\parallel\!Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> as above.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, invoke the variance upper bound that incorporates the controlled leakage (Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma E.2 (Variance under sparsity). ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A5.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)\leq\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)\leq w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}+\big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>eff</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)\leq\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)\leq w_{\mathcal{S}}\,M_{h}^{2}+\big(M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Taking square-roots and using <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{x+y}\leq\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mi>y</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{x+y}\leq\sqrt{x}+\sqrt{y}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}\leq\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)}\leq\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>Var</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>eff</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}(f)}\leq\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q}^{\mathrm{eff}}(f)}\leq\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Combine the last two displays to obtain</p>
<table id="A5.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(P_{1})\leq\lambda\,\Big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\Big)\,\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\!\parallel\!Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mpadded><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P_{1})\leq\lambda\,\Big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\Big)\,\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\!\parallel\!Q)}+C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This establishes both bounds with the left-hand side written as the expected code-length change <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L(P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L(P)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="352.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 352.29" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,352.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 346.38 C 0 349.64 2.64 352.29 5.91 352.29 L 555.16 352.29 C 558.43 352.29 561.07 349.64 561.07 346.38 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 346.38 C 1.97 348.56 3.73 350.32 5.91 350.32 L 555.16 350.32 C 557.34 350.32 559.1 348.56 559.1 346.38 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 332.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:23.28em;font-size:10pt;" height="331.75" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Multi-step code-length change bounds)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(Q_{t})_{t=0}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(Q_{t})_{t=0}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be obtained by repeated log-space tilting steps
<math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}\mapsto Q_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↦</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}\mapsto Q_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> with weights <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> (per-prefix interpolation),
and write</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P)\ :=\ \mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{T})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{0}),\qquad\Lambda_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t},\qquad S_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P)\ :=\ \mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{T})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{0}),\qquad\Lambda_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t},\qquad S_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Then there exist constants <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> such that:</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Domain performance improvement on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em></span>
<span id="A5.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big(\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q_{t+1})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q_{t})\Big)\leq-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\Big)\ +\ C_{2}\,S_{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Big(\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q_{t+1})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q_{t})\Big)\leq-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\Big)\ +\ C_{2}\,S_{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In particular, if </span><math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (oracle targets), then</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\ \leq\ -\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})\ +\ C_{2}\,S_{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\ \leq\ -\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})\ +\ C_{2}\,S_{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">General performance degradation on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</em><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
Let</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H_{T}\ :=\ \sup_{0\leq t&lt;T}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}\quad(&lt;\infty\text{ under small-step updates and }\mathrm{KL}(P_{1}\|Q_{0})\ll 1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.778em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em">:=</mo><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></munder><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000"> under small-step updates and </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≪</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{T}\ :=\ \sup_{0\leq t&lt;T}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}\quad(&lt;\infty\text{ under small-step updates and }\mathrm{KL}(P_{1}\|Q_{0})\ll 1).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Then</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T}\ \leq\ H_{T}\Big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\Big)\,\Lambda_{T}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Var</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.722em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T}\ \leq\ H_{T}\Big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\Big)\,\Lambda_{T}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where the last inequality uses the effective variance bound from Lemma </span><a href="#A5.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma E.2 (Variance under sparsity). ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, applied uniformly over </span><math id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.Thmtheorem3.p3.3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each step <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma E.1 (First-order change of code length under tilting). ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> gives, for any <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{t+1})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{t})=-\,\lambda_{t}\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda_{t}^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})+O(\lambda_{t}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{t+1})-\mathrm{KL}(P\|Q_{t})=-\,\lambda_{t}\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big)+\tfrac{\lambda_{t}^{2}}{2}\,\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})+O(\lambda_{t}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Summing over <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0,\dots,T-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0,\dots,T-1</annotation></semantics></math> and absorbing <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}O(\lambda_{t}^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}O(\lambda_{t}^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> into a constant multiple of <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda_{t}|\leq\lambda_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda_{t}|\leq\lambda_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) yields the generic decomposition</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P)\leq-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big)+C\,S_{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P)\leq-\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\big(\mathbb{E}_{P}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big)+C\,S_{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Domain term (<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>).</em><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text"> By Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma E.3. ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a>,
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q_{t})+\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|\tilde{P}_{2})\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|\tilde{P}_{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]=\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|Q_{t})+\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|\tilde{P}_{2})\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|\tilde{P}_{2})-\mathrm{KL}(P_{2}\|\tilde{P}_{2}).</annotation></semantics></math>
Multiplying by <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\lambda_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\lambda_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and summing gives the first display, with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> absorbing the quadratic/cubic remainders. In the oracle case <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p7.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{P_{2}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\geq\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>,
hence the stated inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">General term (<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>).</em><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text"> The change-of-measure bound with centering gives, for each <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big|\ \leq\ \sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}\ \sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ \leq\ H_{T}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big|\ \leq\ \sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}\ \sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ \leq\ H_{T}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, by applying <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-(\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}])\leq\big|\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-(\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}])\leq\big|\mathbb{E}_{P_{1}}[f_{t}]-\mathbb{E}_{Q_{t}}[f_{t}]\big|</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\,\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\,\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, apply Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma E.2 (Variance under sparsity). ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a> uniformly in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to bound
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ \leq\ \sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ \leq\ \sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>
and factor out <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="205.73" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 205.73" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,205.73) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 199.82 C 0 203.08 2.64 205.73 5.91 205.73 L 555.16 205.73 C 558.43 205.73 561.07 203.08 561.07 199.82 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 199.82 C 1.97 202 3.73 203.76 5.91 203.76 L 555.16 203.76 C 557.34 203.76 559.1 202 559.1 199.82 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 185.85)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.69em;font-size:10pt;" height="185.19" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.4</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smaller steps yield a smaller general performance degradaton bound at a equal domain performance gain)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix a desired domain improvement <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\star}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\star}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\leq-\Delta_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\leq-\Delta_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Among all <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-step tilting schedules that achieve this target, the <em id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">minimal</em> upper bound on the increase of code length on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}\ +\ \Big(\frac{A\,C_{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}+\frac{C_{1}}{\mu_{T}^{2}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.722em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.722em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}\ +\ \Big(\frac{A\,C_{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}+\frac{C_{1}}{\mu_{T}^{2}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{T}:=\inf_{t&lt;T}\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.1389em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">KL</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{T}:=\inf_{t&lt;T}\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=H_{T}\big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=H_{T}\big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed value under the total number of update steps <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and the desired domain gain <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The upper bound strictly decreases as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> increases. Thus, under the equal-steps schedule that attains the target, the per-step effective weight scales as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}\propto 1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}\propto 1/T</annotation></semantics></math>; thus, for the same domain gain, larger <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> implies smaller per-step updates. Hence, smaller step size <math id="A5.Thmtheorem4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> smaller upper bound.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">We work in the oracle case <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>P</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{P}_{2}=P_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the multi-step bound,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\ \leq\ -\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})\ +\ C_{2}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2}\ \leq\ -\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}+C_{2}\,S_{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\ \leq\ -\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})\ +\ C_{2}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2}\ \leq\ -\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}+C_{2}\,S_{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}=\sum_{t}\lambda_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}=\sum_{t}\lambda_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}=\sum_{t}\lambda_{t}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}=\sum_{t}\lambda_{t}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu_{T}:=\inf_{t&lt;T}\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{T}:=\inf_{t&lt;T}\mathrm{KL}(Q_{t}\|P_{2})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus any schedule that achieves <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\leq-\Delta_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{2})\leq-\Delta_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> must satisfy the feasibility constraint</span></p>
<table id="A5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}-C_{2}\,S_{T}\ \geq\ \Delta_{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}-C_{2}\,S_{T}\ \geq\ \Delta_{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">For the general-performance side, the multi-step bound gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\Lambda_{T}+C_{1}\,S_{T}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\Lambda_{T}+C_{1}\,S_{T},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:=H_{T}\big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>w</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:=H_{T}\big(\sqrt{w_{\mathcal{S}}}\,M_{h}+M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}\big)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{T}:=\sup_{t&lt;T}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{T}:=\sup_{t&lt;T}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">For any fixed <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, Cauchy–Schwarz implies <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}\geq\Lambda_{T}^{2}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}\geq\Lambda_{T}^{2}/T</annotation></semantics></math>, with equality iff <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}\equiv\Lambda_{T}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}\equiv\Lambda_{T}/T</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence the bound equation <a href="#A5.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> is minimized (for fixed <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,\Lambda_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,\Lambda_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>) by the equal-steps schedule; moreover, equal steps minimize the feasibility penalty in equation <a href="#A5.E9" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> as well. Under equal steps <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}=\Lambda_{T}^{2}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}=\Lambda_{T}^{2}/T</annotation></semantics></math>, the feasibility constraint becomes the concave quadratic inequality</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}-\frac{C_{2}}{T}\,\Lambda_{T}^{2}\ \geq\ \Delta_{\star}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}-\frac{C_{2}}{T}\,\Lambda_{T}^{2}\ \geq\ \Delta_{\star}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Its smallest feasible solution (the smaller root) is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}^{\min}\ =\ \frac{T}{2C_{2}}\Big(\mu_{T}-\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\tfrac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{T}}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}^{\min}\ =\ \frac{T}{2C_{2}}\Big(\mu_{T}-\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\tfrac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{T}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">which exists for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}/\mu_{T}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}/\mu_{T}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}^{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}^{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}=(\Lambda_{T}^{\min})^{2}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}=(\Lambda_{T}^{\min})^{2}/T</annotation></semantics></math> into equation <a href="#A5.E10" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> yields the optimal-in-this-bound upper bound.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">To expose the dependence on <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, expand the smaller root for large <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}-\frac{C_{2}}{T}\,\Lambda_{T}^{2}=\Delta_{\star}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{T}\,\Lambda_{T}-\frac{C_{2}}{T}\,\Lambda_{T}^{2}=\Delta_{\star},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">the smaller root is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}^{\min}=\frac{T}{2C_{2}}\left(\mu_{T}-\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\frac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{T}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}^{\min}=\frac{T}{2C_{2}}\left(\mu_{T}-\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\frac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{T}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p13.1" class="ltx_p">Set</p>
<table id="A5.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon:=\frac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{T},\qquad x:=\frac{\varepsilon}{\mu_{T}^{2}}=\frac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}^{2}\,T}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon:=\frac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{T},\qquad x:=\frac{\varepsilon}{\mu_{T}^{2}}=\frac{4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}^{2}\,T}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p13.2" class="ltx_p">Then</p>
<table id="A5.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\varepsilon}=\mu_{T}\sqrt{1-x}=\mu_{T}\left(1-\frac{x}{2}-\frac{x^{2}}{8}+O(x^{3})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\varepsilon}=\mu_{T}\sqrt{1-x}=\mu_{T}\left(1-\frac{x}{2}-\frac{x^{2}}{8}+O(x^{3})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p13.3" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A5.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{T}-\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\varepsilon}=\mu_{T}\left(\frac{x}{2}+\frac{x^{2}}{8}+O(x^{3})\right)=\frac{\varepsilon}{2\mu_{T}}+\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{8\mu_{T}^{3}}+O\!\left(\frac{\varepsilon^{3}}{\mu_{T}^{5}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>5</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{T}-\sqrt{\mu_{T}^{2}-\varepsilon}=\mu_{T}\left(\frac{x}{2}+\frac{x^{2}}{8}+O(x^{3})\right)=\frac{\varepsilon}{2\mu_{T}}+\frac{\varepsilon^{2}}{8\mu_{T}^{3}}+O\!\left(\frac{\varepsilon^{3}}{\mu_{T}^{5}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p13.4" class="ltx_p">Multiplying by the prefactor <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T/(2C_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T/(2C_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and substituting <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=4C_{2}\Delta_{\star}/T</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}^{\min}=\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}+\frac{C_{2}\,\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{T}+O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>min</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}^{\min}=\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}+\frac{C_{2}\,\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}\cdot\frac{1}{T}+O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}\ +\ \Big(\frac{A\,C_{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}+\frac{C_{1}}{\mu_{T}^{2}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ A\,\frac{\Delta_{\star}}{\mu_{T}}\ +\ \Big(\frac{A\,C_{2}}{\mu_{T}^{3}}+\frac{C_{1}}{\mu_{T}^{2}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\star}^{2}}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15.2.1" class="ltx_text">which decreases strictly in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> and converges to <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\,\Delta_{\star}/\mu_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\,\Delta_{\star}/\mu_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p16.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="252.77" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 252.77" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,252.77) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(-5.53,0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#292074;" fill="#292074" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 246.87 C 0 250.13 2.64 252.77 5.91 252.77 L 555.16 252.77 C 558.43 252.77 561.07 250.13 561.07 246.87 L 561.07 5.91 C 561.07 2.64 558.43 0 555.16 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F6F5FC;" fill="#F6F5FC" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 246.87 C 1.97 249.04 3.73 250.8 5.91 250.8 L 555.16 250.8 C 557.34 250.8 559.1 249.04 559.1 246.87 L 559.1 5.91 C 559.1 3.73 557.34 1.97 555.16 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 10.27 232.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:39.06em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:16.09em;font-size:10pt;" height="232.23" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="540.48"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p16.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:39.06em;">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.5</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Label-only supervision enlarges the safe per-step range)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Define</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{s}\ :=\ \sqrt{\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[s\,M_{h}^{2}+(m-s)\,M_{e}^{2}\big]\ },\qquad M_{e}:=M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.778em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{s}\ :=\ \sqrt{\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[s\,M_{h}^{2}+(m-s)\,M_{e}^{2}\big]\ },\qquad M_{e}:=M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> is the expected number of hard tokens per example on <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the example token length.
For any <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>-step <em id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">equal-steps</em> schedule (<math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}\equiv\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}\equiv\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), a general-performance degradation <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\leq\varepsilon_{\rm fg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fg</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\leq\varepsilon_{\rm fg}</annotation></semantics></math> is ensured whenever the per-step effective weight satisfies</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\ \leq\ \lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ :=\ \frac{-\,H_{T}V_{s}+\sqrt{(H_{T}V_{s})^{2}+\tfrac{4C_{1}}{T}\,\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}}{2C_{1}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.778em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fg</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.170em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\ \leq\ \lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ :=\ \frac{-\,H_{T}V_{s}+\sqrt{(H_{T}V_{s})^{2}+\tfrac{4C_{1}}{T}\,\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}}{2C_{1}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In particular, as <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> grows,</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ =\ \frac{\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}{H_{T}V_{s}}\cdot\frac{1}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fg</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.722em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ =\ \frac{\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}{H_{T}V_{s}}\cdot\frac{1}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">so the <em id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.4.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">safe per-step range</em> widens inversely with <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{e}\ll M_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≪</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{e}\ll M_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{s}\asymp M_{h}\sqrt{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≍</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{s}\asymp M_{h}\sqrt{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence</span></span>
<span id="A5.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(s)\ \asymp\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{s}}\quad\text{(for fixed }\varepsilon_{\rm fg},H_{T},M_{h},T)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.778em">≍</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">(for fixed </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">fg</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(s)\ \asymp\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{s}}\quad\text{(for fixed }\varepsilon_{\rm fg},H_{T},M_{h},T).</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Therefore, if label-only supervision reduces <math id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> relative to chain-of-thought, it <em id="A5.Thmtheorem5.p1.5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">strictly enlarges</em> the admissible per-step range.</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{e}:=M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{e}:=M_{l}+(\beta+\gamma)M_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>. From Lemma <a href="#A5.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma E.2 (Variance under sparsity). ‣ Notation. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.2</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{a\sim Q_{t}}[f_{t}(a)^{2}]\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S},t}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ (1-w_{\mathcal{S},t})\,M_{e}^{2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}_{a\sim Q_{t}}[f_{t}(a)^{2}]\ \leq\ w_{\mathcal{S},t}\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ (1-w_{\mathcal{S},t})\,M_{e}^{2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider sampling an example <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, with response length <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(z)\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(z)\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(z)\subseteq\{1,\dots,m(z)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(z)\subseteq\{1,\dots,m(z)\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of hard positions for that example, with cardinality <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(z)=|J(z)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(z)=|J(z)|</annotation></semantics></math>.
If we (conceptually) select a token position uniformly at random along the generated path, then the probability of landing in the hard set equals the <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">hard fraction</em>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{\mathcal{S},t}\ =\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{s(z)}{m(z)}\right]\ =:\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{\mathcal{S},t}\ =\ \mathbb{E}\!\left[\frac{s(z)}{m(z)}\right]\ =:\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the expectation is over the (data-induced) randomness of examples and the path under <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Substituting equation <a href="#A5.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> into equation <a href="#A5.E11" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ \Big(1-\mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\Big)\,M_{e}^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ \Big(1-\mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\Big)\,M_{e}^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.3.1" class="ltx_text">We now relax the hard fraction into an affine form in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s,m)</annotation></semantics></math> that pairs naturally with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M_{h}^{2},M_{e}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M_{h}^{2},M_{e}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m(z)\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m(z)\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq s(z)\leq m(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq s(z)\leq m(z)</annotation></semantics></math> for every example,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{s(z)}{m(z)}\ \leq\ s(z),\qquad 1-\frac{s(z)}{m(z)}\ \leq\ m(z)-s(z)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{s(z)}{m(z)}\ \leq\ s(z),\qquad 1-\frac{s(z)}{m(z)}\ \leq\ m(z)-s(z).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations and using linearity,</span></p>
<table id="A5.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ \Big(1-\mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\Big)\,M_{e}^{2}\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[s\,M_{h}^{2}+(m-s)\,M_{e}^{2}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\,M_{h}^{2}\ +\ \Big(1-\mathbb{E}\!\big[\tfrac{s}{m}\big]\Big)\,M_{e}^{2}\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[s\,M_{h}^{2}+(m-s)\,M_{e}^{2}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.5.1" class="ltx_text">Combining equation <a href="#A5.E13" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> and equation <a href="#A5.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> gives the <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.5.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">uniform (in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p18.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>)</em> token-level bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ \leq\ \sqrt{\,\mathbb{E}\!\big[s\,M_{h}^{2}+(m-s)\,M_{e}^{2}\big]\,}\ :=\ V_{s},\qquad\text{for all }t=0,1,\dots,T-1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><msqrt><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">:=</mo><mi>V</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>s</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>for all </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ \leq\ \sqrt{\,\mathbb{E}\!\big[s\,M_{h}^{2}+(m-s)\,M_{e}^{2}\big]\,}\ :=\ V_{s},\qquad\text{for all }t=0,1,\dots,T-1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">The general-performance part of Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem E.3 (Multi-step code-length change bounds). ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.3</span></a> states that</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ +\ C_{1}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2},\qquad H_{T}\ :=\ \sup_{0\leq t&lt;T}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></munder><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}\,\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}_{Q_{t}}(f_{t})}\ +\ C_{1}\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2},\qquad H_{T}\ :=\ \sup_{0\leq t&lt;T}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P_{1}\|Q_{t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using equation <a href="#A5.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, we obtain the uniform (in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>) upper bound</span></p>
<table id="A5.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\,V_{s}\,\Lambda_{T}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T},\qquad\Lambda_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t},\ \ S_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ H_{T}\,V_{s}\,\Lambda_{T}\ +\ C_{1}\,S_{T},\qquad\Lambda_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t},\ \ S_{T}:=\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\lambda_{t}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">For an equal-steps schedule <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t}\equiv\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t}\equiv\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{T}=T\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{T}=T\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{T}=T\lambda^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{T}=T\lambda^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence from equation <a href="#A5.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a></span></p>
<table id="A5.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ T\Big(H_{T}\,V_{s}\,\lambda\ +\ C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\ \leq\ T\Big(H_{T}\,V_{s}\,\lambda\ +\ C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">Impose a general-performance budget <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\leq\varepsilon_{\rm fg}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>fg</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta L_{T}(P_{1})\leq\varepsilon_{\rm fg}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then equation <a href="#A5.E17" title="In Proof. ‣ General performance degradation on 𝒟_1. ‣ E.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix E Additional Definitions, Theorems and Proof ‣ SFT Doesn’t Always Hurt General Capabilities: Revisiting Domain-Specific Fine-Tuning in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> yields the quadratic constraint</span></p>
<table id="A5.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}\ +\ (H_{T}V_{s})\,\lambda\ -\ \frac{\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}{T}\ \leq\ 0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>fg</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}\,\lambda^{2}\ +\ (H_{T}V_{s})\,\lambda\ -\ \frac{\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}{T}\ \leq\ 0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.3.1" class="ltx_text">The feasible interval in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\,0,\ \lambda_{\max}(T;s)\,]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\,0,\ \lambda_{\max}(T;s)\,]</annotation></semantics></math>, where the positive root is</span></p>
<table id="A5.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ =\ \frac{-\,H_{T}V_{s}\ +\ \sqrt{(H_{T}V_{s})^{2}\ +\ \tfrac{4C_{1}}{T}\,\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}}{2C_{1}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>fg</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ =\ \frac{-\,H_{T}V_{s}\ +\ \sqrt{(H_{T}V_{s})^{2}\ +\ \tfrac{4C_{1}}{T}\,\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}}{2C_{1}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.4.1" class="ltx_text">A first-order expansion in <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/T</annotation></semantics></math> (Taylor for <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{a^{2}+\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{a^{2}+\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sim T^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sim T^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>) gives</span></p>
<table id="A5.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ =\ \frac{\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}{H_{T}\,V_{s}}\cdot\frac{1}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big),\quad\text{as }T\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>fg</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ =\ \frac{\varepsilon_{\rm fg}}{H_{T}\,V_{s}}\cdot\frac{1}{T}\ +\ O\!\Big(\frac{1}{T^{2}}\Big),\quad\text{as }T\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.5.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, when <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{e}\ll M_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>≪</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{e}\ll M_{h}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{e}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{e}</annotation></semantics></math>-term is negligible and
<math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{s}=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[s]\,M_{h}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[m-s]\,M_{e}^{2}}\ \approx\ M_{h}\,\sqrt{s}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{s}=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[s]\,M_{h}^{2}+\mathbb{E}[m-s]\,M_{e}^{2}}\ \approx\ M_{h}\,\sqrt{s},</annotation></semantics></math>
so</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ \asymp\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{s}}\qquad(\text{for fixed }\varepsilon_{\rm fg},\,H_{T},\,M_{h},T)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≍</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>s</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>for fixed </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>fg</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\max}(T;s)\ \asymp\ \frac{1}{\sqrt{s}}\qquad(\text{for fixed }\varepsilon_{\rm fg},\,H_{T},\,M_{h},T).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.6.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.6.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reducing <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math></em> (as is typical under label-only supervision versus chain-of-thought) <em id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.6.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">strictly enlarges</em> the admissible per-step range, and the range also increases with <math id="A5.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p20.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
